"body": "A shared page that waits for a click showed a black box in its preview card (the fireworks page, seen on the live site).\n\nOnly when the viewer is inside a card, and only when the page's own words say click or tap, the page gets a tap every few seconds (41 at most). The taps run inside the same locked frame as the page, so nothing about what the page can reach changes. They stop the moment a person touches it. Opened on its own, the page is untouched.\n\nLocal build: fireworks preview now moves; the basketball page takes its shot ('Swish! 1 / 1').",
